{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>וָאוֹצִאָה</b> — thus it is written, for the alef is a root letter of the verb, on the pattern of וָאָבוֹאָה. וָאֲצַוֶּה is qere, for the near form is the shorter way." "<b>עַל אָדוֹ הָרֹאשׁ</b> — for he is head in Casiphia, the place." "<b>אֶל אָדוֹ אָחִיו</b> — missing a vav. The correct reading is אֶל אָדוֹ וְאָחִיו, for they are temple servants. Some say: that אָחִיו is the name of the brother of Ado, or his kinsman."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:16.313262888Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}